ubertooth (2020-12-R1+modern1) unstable; urgency=low

  New features:
  * ubertooth-util: add -H / --host-version to print the installed host tools
    (libubertooth) version and git revision, without needing a device
    (distinct from -v firmware revision and -V firmware compile info)

  Build fixes:
  * Fix build with CMake 4.x: update cmake_minimum_required to VERSION 3.5...3.27
    in host/CMakeLists.txt, host/misc/CMakeLists.txt, host/misc/udev/CMakeLists.txt
    (upstream issue #551)
  * Fix build with Python 3.12+: replace deprecated distutils.core with setuptools
    in host/python/specan_ui/setup.py and host/python/specan_ui/setup.py.in
    Credit: Arnaud Rebillout <arnaudr@kali.org> (Kali Linux fork)
  * Fix InvalidVersion error in new setuptools versions: set version='1' in
    specan_ui setup.py and add set(PACKAGE_VERSION 1) to specan_ui CMakeLists.txt
    Credit: Rhys Perry <rhysperry111@gmail.com> (upstream PR #524)
  * CMakeLists: use message(FATAL_ERROR ...) instead of message(FATAL ...), and
    CACHE STRING instead of CACHE INT for the version variables
  * Guard MAX/MIN macros in ubertooth_control.h with #ifndef to avoid
    -Wmacro-redefined against the system <sys/param.h>
  * specan_ui: remove the stale committed setup.py (generated from setup.py.in
    by CMake); the template is now the single source of truth

  Robustness fixes (host, this fork):
  * libubertooth: ubertooth_count() now returns int and propagates a negative
    error from libusb_init instead of wrapping to a large unsigned value
  * libubertooth: ubertooth_start() frees its allocation on the connect-failure
    path (was a leak); ubertooth_stop() guards devh before libusb_close and
    does not call libusb_exit(NULL) on the failed-connect path
  * libubertooth: find_ubertooth_device() sets devh=NULL on a single-device
    open failure; removed a shadowed variable
  * ubertooth-dfu / ubertooth-ducky: check fread() return values
    (-Wunused-result); error out on a short read instead of using partial data

  Documentation:
  * ubertooth-util man page: document that -U selects by USB enumeration
    index (not serial, not stable) and how to disambiguate devices (serial
    listing / -I LED flash); add a SELECTING A DEVICE section
  * Man-page accuracy pass across all host tool pages (both host/doc/*.md ronn
    sources and host/doc/man/*.1 roff): convert H1s to ronn `name(1) -- desc`
    form; bump .TH dates to October 2026; fix ubertooth-debug NAME (was wrongly
    copied from rx; it reads/writes CC2400 registers); fix ubertooth.7 "IRC
    channel on Discord" -> "channel on Discord" and add the missing
    ubertooth-follow/-tx/-ducky catalog entries; fix ubertooth-rx synopsis
    `-u <uap>` and "piocnets" typo; remove a stray quote in ubertooth-dump;
    fix ubertooth-specan `##EXAMPLES` heading; relabel ubertooth-afh `-m` as a
    channel-removal count (not seconds) and note `-a` is non-functional; fix
    ubertooth-btle "futher" typo. Document previously-undocumented real flags:
    rx `-s` (deprecated no-op), btle `-j`/`-J` (jamming), follow `-d <file>`,
    ego `-j`/`-l <1-48>`/`-a <access_code>`, ducky `-s` (sarcasm easter egg).
    ronn was unavailable; the committed .1 files were hand-synced to match.
  * ubertooth-util man page: replace placeholder SYNOPSIS with the real flag
    summary, add -H/--host-version, fix a typo; make host/doc/*.md the single
    source and optionally regenerate roff .1 via ronn (committed .1 are the
    fallback when ronn is absent)
  * Add a command-line tool catalog (grouped by purpose, with per-tool doc
    links) to README.md and docs/source/software.rst
  * Add COMPATIBILITY.md (supported OS/toolchain/Python matrix) and per-tool
    man pages for ubertooth-follow, ubertooth-tx, and ubertooth-ducky
  * Add docs/source/Release_2020-12-R1.rst; annotate and prune the inherited
    upstream ToDo list; note the ubertooth-btbr hang in firmware/btbr/README.md

  Continuous integration:
  * Drop macos-13 (Intel) from the CI matrix: GitHub's Intel runners queue
    unreliably and stalled runs; arm64 macOS 14/15/26 remain covered and Intel
    is documented as expected-to-build but unverified (COMPATIBILITY.md)
  * Modernize CI: pinned OS matrix (Ubuntu 20.04/22.04/24.04, macOS 14/15/26)
    with ubuntu-latest and Fedora soft-fail canaries, firmware build in CI,
    actions/checkout@v4, host CLI + Python import smoke tests, firmware artifacts

  Bug fixes (this fork):
  * ubertooth-util -I (identify): install a SIGINT handler so Ctrl-C turns
    the USR/RX/TX LEDs off before exit, instead of leaving them lit

  Bug fixes (cherry-picked from community forks):
  * Fix divide-by-zero in bluetooth.c AFH hop selection when used_channels < 20
    Credit: Kielukel <93320945+Kielukel@users.noreply.github.com>
    Origin: https://github.com/Kielukel/ubertooth
  * Fix divide-by-zero in btbr/hop.c when chan_count is 0
    Credit: Piotr Wasylów <piotr@wasylow.com>
    Origin: https://github.com/Kielukel/ubertooth

  Bug fixes (cherry-picked from upstream open PRs):
  * Fix CRC verify not filtering bad-CRC packets in ubertooth-btle -v1 mode;
    add on-device CRC verification in LE PHY engine (upstream PR #550)
    Credit: oliver <icetzsr@gmail.com>
  * Fix rssi_iir_update() and rssi_get_avg() channel checks in ubertooth_rssi.c
    (upstream PR #481)
    Credit: Gabriele Gristina <matrix@users.noreply.github.com>
  * Fix ubertooth-dfu variable in firmware build (upstream PR #485)
    Credit: Michael Ossmann <mike@ossmann.com>
  * Improved Paging process speed and reliability (upstream PR #540)
    Credit: Hillel Chimowicz <hllhll@users.noreply.github.com>

  Other improvements (cherry-picked from upstream open PRs):
  * Update scapy usage to PcapReader (deprecated API removal) (upstream PR #519)
    Credit: stryngs <support@configitnow.com>
  * Update CI scripts and Docker image for Ubuntu 22.04 (upstream PR #521)
    Credit: linux4life798

  Known open issues not yet addressed:
  * ubertooth-btbr hangs after start (upstream issue #520)
  * Memory leaks in libubertooth and ubertooth-scan (upstream issues #542, #543)
  * LE packets truncated to 50 bytes (upstream issue #468)
  * Channel -1 bug when setting channel 1 (upstream issue #448)

 -- community fork  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:00:00 -0700

